{
  "an10.30:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 10.30 ",
  "an10.30:0.2": "3. The Great Chapter ",
  "an10.30:0.3": "Kosala (2nd) ",
  "an10.30:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an10.30:1.2": "Now at that time King Pasenadi of Kosala returned from combat after winning a battle and succeeding in his strategy. ",
  "an10.30:1.3": "Then King Pasenadi of Kosala went to the monastery. ",
  "an10.30:1.4": "He went by carriage as far as the terrain allowed, then descended and entered the monastery on foot. ",
  "an10.30:1.5": "At that time several mendicants were walking mindfully in the open air. ",
  "an10.30:1.6": "Then King Pasenadi of Kosala went up to them and said, ",
  "an10.30:1.7": "“Sirs, where is the Blessed One at present, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha? ",
  "an10.30:1.8": "For I want to see the Buddha.” ",
  "an10.30:1.9": "“Great king, that’s his dwelling, with the door closed. Approach it quietly, without hurrying; go onto the porch, clear your throat, and knock on the door-panel. The Buddha will open the door.” ",
  "an10.30:2.1": "So the king approached the Buddha’s dwelling, cleared his throat and knocked on the door-panel, and the Buddha opened the door. ",
  "an10.30:2.2": "Then King Pasenadi entered the Buddha’s dwelling. He bowed with his head to the Buddha’s feet, caressing them and covering them with kisses, and pronounced his name: ",
  "an10.30:2.3": "“Sir, I am Pasenadi, king of Kosal